{
 "_about": "MANDATE prototype role catalogue (declared mandates). A tool's resource sensitivity: 0 public, 1 internal, 2 personal/financial, 3 restricted (HR salary). source=untrusted means the output can carry third-party content (indirect prompt injection vector). Destinations: 'internal' or an external host pattern. E2 additions: max_per_window/budget_window_s (effect budgets), max_identical_per_window (duplicate consequential actions), trusted_store (writes create content others will trust; under taint they are provenance-labelled untrusted), role max_rate_per_min (declared action-rate ceiling). E3 additions: read_budget per role (per_600s / per_3600s / sensitive_unique) with per-task overrides; object_arg + field_arg for object-level authorization; spend_arg for cumulative spend limits; task_meta (purpose, allowed fields, bulk) per role task. E4 additions: read_budget per_86400s (cumulative daily reads), distinct_per_day / distinct_per_week (distinct objects), enforced per agent AND on a shared pool per (root principal, dataset); task_meta.pool_agents sizes the pool for owner-declared multi-agent tasks. E4.2 additions: tools.*.requires_corroboration (a trusted read of that resource must follow the last untrusted input before the action); datasets.* = dataset-owner quota across ALL principals (per_600s, distinct_per_day), enforced as a fair share: when exceeded, only principals above total/active-principals are gated. E4.2.1: datasets.*.ceiling_multiplier (hard dataset ceiling, default 2); tools.*.corroboration_arg (default 'service'). E4.3.1 additions: workspace (owner-provided, sanitized documents for the console workbench). read_workspace_doc is an untrusted source (third-party content), scanned by the injection detector; list_workspace_docs returns file names only.",
